## Step 8: Handle ACF repeaters and flexible fields safely

Repeater:

```php
<?php if ( function_exists( 'have_rows' ) && have_rows( 'faq_items' ) ) : ?>
	<div class="faq">
		<?php while ( have_rows( 'faq_items' ) ) : ?>
			<?php the_row(); ?>
			<?php
			$question = get_sub_field( 'question' );
			$answer   = get_sub_field( 'answer' );
			?>

			<?php if ( $question || $answer ) : ?>
				<details class="faq__item">
					<?php if ( $question ) : ?>
						<summary class="faq__question"><?php echo esc_html( $question ); ?></summary>
					<?php endif; ?>

					<?php if ( $answer ) : ?>
						<div class="faq__answer"><?php echo wp_kses_post( $answer ); ?></div>
					<?php endif; ?>
				</details>
			<?php endif; ?>
		<?php endwhile; ?>
	</div>
<?php endif; ?>
```

Relationship field:

```php
<?php
$projects = theme_get_acf_field( 'featured_projects', false, array() );
?>

<?php if ( is_array( $projects ) && $projects ) : ?>
	<section class="featured-projects">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="card-grid">
				<?php foreach ( $projects as $project ) : ?>
					<?php
					$project_id = is_object( $project ) ? $project->ID : (int) $project;

					get_template_part(
						'template-parts/content/content',
						'project-card',
						array( 'post_id' => $project_id )
					);
					?>
				<?php endforeach; ?>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
<?php endif; ?>
```

Template part accepting `$args`:

```php
<?php
$post_id = isset( $args['post_id'] ) ? (int) $args['post_id'] : get_the_ID();

if ( ! $post_id ) {
	return;
}
?>

<article class="card">
	<a class="card__link" href="<?php echo esc_url( get_permalink( $post_id ) ); ?>">
		<?php
		if ( has_post_thumbnail( $post_id ) ) {
			echo get_the_post_thumbnail(
				$post_id,
				'medium_large',
				array( 'class' => 'card__image' )
			);
		}
		?>

		<h3 class="card__title"><?php echo esc_html( get_the_title( $post_id ) ); ?></h3>
	</a>
</article>
```

## Step 9: Write plain CSS

Start with foundation CSS and add components only as templates require them.

`assets/css/main.css`:

```css
:root {
